# The realmtools image is built with `context: ..` — the repository root. Without this file the
# ENTIRE working tree is sent to the Docker daemon on every build: hundreds of megabytes of runtime
# state, and, on a remote or rootless context, over a socket or the network.
#
# Allowlist, not denylist. A new directory of local state should be excluded by default rather than
# shipped because nobody remembered to add it.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!src/

# …minus anything that regenerates inside the allowed paths
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.py[cod]
src/**/.mypy_cache/
src/**/.ruff_cache/
